  "findings": [
    "Runs on Windows unmodified; ~102 generated fps compiled (paper: 96), 78 fps eager.",
    "Lip-sync clearly better than FLOAT on every clip: mean LSE-C 7.88-7.92 vs 6.47 streamed FLOAT; LSE-D 7.35 vs 8.20.",
    "A short first hop (8 frames, window still ends at the newest audio, last 8 frames kept) costs no lip-sync (7.92) and brings the first frame to ~0.56 s after audio start (upstream 1.2 s).",
    "2 denoise steps: 177 ms per chunk, LSE-C 7.42, but visibly washed out with ghosted eyes; 4 steps needed.",
    "GPU time per audio second 0.25 (4 steps) vs FLOAT 0.14, about 1.8x; each reply also costs one extra chunk for the short first hop.",
    "Peak VRAM 4.9/5.4-5.6 GB and process commit ~10 GB vs FLOAT 2.8 GB / 6.7 GB. Commit follows VRAM on Windows.",
    "Silence renders a natural closed-mouth idle with slight head motion; blinks happen on their own while speaking.",
    "Not measured: loaded runs with TTS/STT/LLM resident (contention, commit headroom on a real call)."
